A||||21||Adrift||$400 to spend on a sound system: What should I buy?||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||07-08-2001||09:39 PM||||What is the most cost effective upgrade I could purchase for a fiero ($400 limit?). I don't care if I lose the headrest speakers. A CD Player is a must. I know next to nothing about car stereos, so any links would be a great help. I already checked out fierosound's setup but its a little overkill. I just want a sweet sounding (good highs and lows) system which can also pump out enough volume for those sunroof days. Ideally, I'd like something like the sound system that comes standard on the new Nissan Maximas/Altimas/Pathfinders - they sound awesome!<P>Thanks<BR>Adrift<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-08-2001||10:08 PM||||Ready?<BR>Pioneer DEH-P47DH AM/FM/CD $229<BR>2 Pairs of TS877 3.5" speakers for seats $56.00 for BOTH pairs. ($28.00 per pair)<BR>TS-A4103 4 X 10 speakers $79.00<P>So $229 + $56 + $79 = $364.00<P>They can be ordered online from:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/</A> <P>How's that?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-08-2001||10:29 PM||||That's pretty good there Orief... <P>I dunno if anyone saw this yet, but I just saw a Kenwood Cd reciever in the Wiz ad this weekend. It's got a faceplate that the display is tunable to 50-something colors!!!! It's like $250 or so. It looks cool. but I already have my Sony X-Pold head unit and I love that. $350||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||07-08-2001||11:12 PM||||Oreif - that was amazing, A true talent!<BR>Two Questions:<BR>A)TS877 & TS-A4103 - Are these Pioneer speakers? If not, what brand are they?<BR>b)No subwoofer?<P>c)Good canadian dealer to buy these at? (I know you can't probably help me with this one... :{)<P>Thank you,<BR>Adrift<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||07-08-2001||11:17 PM||||I would also recommend going to Best Buy and picking up an adapter harness for a 1982 thru 1988 GM. This will plug into the cars harness and give instructions how to attach to the Pioneer radio. Makes install VERY easy. They run about $8-$12.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Adrift||07-08-2001||11:27 PM||||As far as I know, Best buy isn't in Canada (yet!). I'm sure I can find something similar here though..<P>One last question - any reason why I shouldn't try to buy these used (ebay/local classifieds)? Do speakers/CD Players "burn-out" or degrade drastically over time?<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Ari<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||07-08-2001||11:52 PM||||You could probably get a factory CD player out of a Sunfire or other Pontiac (red lighting) for &lt;$150 US.<P>That would preserve the stock look, possibly detering thieves.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierofreek2001||07-09-2001||12:21 AM||||heres my stereo, i really like it, its one of the most attractive ones ive ever seen<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stereo_face_small_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||07-09-2001||12:41 AM||||$400...hmmm...well it depends what kind of cd receiver you want. Onlinecarstereo.com is having a sale on their JVC LX-30 El Kameleon for $199. I've had one for a few months now and love it. It's pretty flashy. 45x4 watt, remote, high- and low-pass filter, 4 sets of pre-outs. One is a sub-out if you wanted to add a subwoofer later. Or if you wanted a subwoofer now, you might want to get a basic CD receiver. Because you would need the sub, and box, an amp, and all the wires to hook it up. I found a good deal on my amp/sub combo. Got a 50x2 MTX amp on eBay for $100, MTX 10" sub on eBay for $60, then made my own box, and bought an amp wiring kit. A total of about $200. Or you could go the easy way and get a Bazooka tube. Monkeyman had one for sell not too long ago. Still might have it.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">      <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000009||DecadenceR||07-09-2001||01:28 AM||||Fierofreek, your radio looks like mine. Which model is yours?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image1_4.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by DecadenceR (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||DecadenceR||07-09-2001||01:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>One last question - any reason why I shouldn't try to buy these used (ebay/local classifieds)? Do speakers/CD Players "burn-out" or degrade drastically over time?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WEll one big reason is you never know how much abuse people put their things through. it's one thing if you know the person and how they treat their equipment.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||07-09-2001||01:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>As far as I know, Best buy isn't in Canada (yet!). I'm sure I can find something similar here though..<P>One last question - any reason why I shouldn't try to buy these used (ebay/local classifieds)? Do speakers/CD Players "burn-out" or degrade drastically over time?<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Ari<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The prices at the above link are about as low as you'll find for new, But if you can get one locally or thru Ebay for less, go for it! Never hurts to save a few $$$. You probably won't find the speakers for less since the specific sized speakers are hard to get anyways. But you could save lots on the stereo. As for the harness adapter, Crutchfield sells them for $10.00. <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com</A> <P>You could also find other stereo's on sale for less but remember that the standard size radio's will require an adapter to fit the opening in the Fiero. The Pioneer listed above is a perfect fit. So if you find a regular one like the JVC that's listed on sale, you still need $20.00 for the adapter kit. The other thing is you would need to compare features with the different units too. The only other thing that could change your opinion is sound. Everyone has their own tastes in how music should sound. You may not like the sound of Pioneer speakers. You could find other brands that sound better to you for about the same price. It's a matter of choice. I have installed and heard many systems in many cars. Some of them I thought they sounded bad for one reason or another but the person who's car it was thought it sounded great. It's their car and they listen to their music. I would suggest going to a few stores near you and listen to various brands. Once you find a stereo that sounds good to you and the associated speakers, search online for the lowest prices. The above list I posted earlier is generally a good sounding set-up  and ease of installation for the price limit. There is always room to expand the system later with amps, subs, crossovers, surround sound, equalizers, etc. The best advice I could give to anyone who wants a stereo system in their car is don't buy what everyone says sounds good, buy what sounds good to you.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||07-09-2001||09:06 AM||||Oreif listed a great budget system that won't dissapoint you. I have an amendment to it however, and I'm sure he'd agree that is a good call.<BR>Replace that DEH-P47-DH with a DEH-77-DH from <A HREF="http://www.competitionsound.com/car-audio-chrysler---gm-fit-decks-pioneer.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.competitionsound.com/car-audio-chrysler---gm-fit-decks-pioneer.html</A> <P>Only $215, plus has front, rear, and sub pre-amp outputs for upgrading in the future, has built-in alarm, remote control, built in crossovers, all kinds of goodies. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||07-09-2001||09:30 AM||||I agree with Stimpy! Save $15.00 and get the upgraded model. The 77 is the same as the 47 just with more features. (listed above)||||reg||14
