Z||000017||DreXteR||07-09-2001||05:40 PM||||Adrift - The fiero is a limited space car for Audio. How good you want to hear = how much $$$.  Well, for a good system in the budget 1st I need to know what kind of "goodies" you want. Goodies are mp3 playback, spectrum anilizer, DSP (is the most awesome thing), cdr reading and more. If you want loud, the fiero is not the case. If you want Hi-Fi (beleive me is the most rewarding) you can do it in a fiero, but maybe be more than 400. But think, is better to spent a lil more for a good system than build a mediocre 1 for be cheap. <P>1st - The head unit is the heart of everithing. Get a good 1, doesnt mean expensive. Ex. DSP, EQ, CD, so on. Dont married with a specific brand, can cost u a fortune. <BR>2nd - Speakers, get the most range can produce. Analize the materials that are buildted. <BR>3rd - Good oxigen free clables. <P>I have a very good experinece in auto sound. I have in mind a good setup that can blow the fealings of anyone, but can be a lil expensive compared to $400. May be near the $700. But you dont need a pair of 10" subs and Hi amps. You can start with the basics.<P>I dont have here the model of the head unit but its +-300 on ebay. It has screen savers, parametric EQ, DSP, In dash CD, AUX (is a must for Nomad Jukebox), and maybe more stuff aI cant remember. Infinity Kappa Speakers, beleiveme are AWESOME. And the trick maker a Creative Nomad Jukebox, holds up to 250cd in mp3, EAX, and its portable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>we talking more than 400 but for sure will be awesome. <P>Well my advise, Infinity Kappa, good oxigen free wires, DONT USE YOUR OLD WIRES make it new with the OxFree, and a good head unit. Phioneers are good and are cheap but consider the one I will install, its a showstoper, imagine you are crusing in the nigth stop for some beers and have some good time with frieds, you turn on the radio and the will want to see what sound so good an BAM! a screensaver in the radio! WOOOOO. hehe<P>Besides have DSP, you can hear your favorite tunes in concert, hall, arena .... its like have a Home theater on you baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Parametric EQ, you dont have to be a engeneer to calibrate the EQ curve to sound good. Motorized fold down face, and the unit color is silver. Just Perfect. IMO.<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000018||Santa Cruzer||07-09-2001||06:50 PM||||Hey adrift go for the one with the motor at least then you'll have something to work with,why waste money on stereo stuff when you need engine work,i used to think like that to until it hit mE.... "TUNE UP'S BEFORE TOY'S"!!<P>------------------<BR>red candy apple copper burgandy color,tan interior all options,american racing rims,Pioneer Cd Player,pioneer 120w speakers"in factory location",sony ****  amp,and workin' on a girl to go with the package <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/me!!!.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
